{"adjusted_val_bpb": 0.5063773543343779, "attempt": 0, "charged": true, "critic": {"issues": ["No sign that the candidate gets around the measurement. It does not read files, use pasted answers, or touch test labels. The new gamma for the RBF kernel is computed only from the training-fold features Za, using a subsample drawn with the seed argument. The meta-learner is still fit on out-of-fold predictions inside the training set, grouped by scaffold.", "No bug that would make the result meaningless. The edit roughly halves the compute: 300 LGB rounds at twice the learning rate, 100 RF trees instead of 200, 3 inner folds instead of 5, and the kernel-ridge grid cut to one setting (lam=0.5, wr=1.0). The one remaining setting is also the default best_cfg, so the selection loop is now trivial but still correct. The median of squared distances as the RBF scale is a standard choice and is valid.", "Recomputed z: (0.4895 - 0.5064) / (0.0042 * sqrt(1/1 + 1/1)) = -0.0169 / 0.00594 = -2.85, which matches the harness value of -2.845. The candidate is about 0.017 worse, which is clearly outside the noise, so the provisional reject is consistent with the numbers.", "Note: the diff gives no runtime figure. If this was meant as a speed-up to free budget for other changes, the cost in loss (about 0.017) is too high. Several changes are bundled together, so the cause of the loss is unclear. Likely causes are the 3 inner folds, which give fewer meta-training rows per fit, and the removed kernel-ridge grid search."], "ok": true, "veto": false}, "decision": "reject", "description": "Cut compute: fewer boosting rounds with higher learning rate, fewer RF trees, a single KRR config (no inner CV grid), and 3 outer stacking folds.", "edit_class": "structural", "flags": [], "gpu": "willow", "idea_id": "b049", "incumbent_after": {"mean": 0.4894866999475836, "n": 1}, "incumbent_before": {"mean": 0.4894866999475836, "n": 1}, "job_id": "B1_lipo_HH_1_cs2-crash_fix-7_1795056795941", "kind": "crash_f